Source package: gtksourceview5

profiler-mark-without-location.patch
    GtkSourceView 5.18 ends every load with a profiler mark naming the file loaded, which it finds with
    g_file_peek_path on the loader's location. A load from a stream, which gtk_source_file_loader_new_from_stream
    creates, has no location, and since Ubuntu builds GtkSourceView with Sysprof support, which evaluates the mark's
    arguments also when no profiler runs, every such load logs two GLib criticals, "g_object_get_qdata: assertion
    'G_IS_OBJECT (object)' failed" and "g_file_get_path: assertion 'G_IS_FILE (file)' failed". Text Editor loads the
    text it reads from standard input (gnome-text-editor -) from a stream. The patch is upstream commit 0efed2a9,
    which passes no file name for a load without a location. Drop it once Ubuntu ships GtkSourceView 5.21.0 or
    later, which have it.

test-file-loader-stream.patch
    Adds /file-loader/stream to testsuite/test-file-loader.c, which loads a memory stream and checks the text. The
    test suite runs during the build, and g_test_init makes criticals fatal there, so the test fails without the patch
    above in a build with Sysprof support. Upstream has no such test. Drop it together with the patch above.

xvfb-noreset.patch (debian-series)
    Keeps the test suite from failing at random with "Failed to open display". debian/rules runs the tests with
    xvfb-run, which starts Xvfb without -noreset, so Xvfb resets whenever its last client disconnects, and drops a
    client which is still setting up its connection then. The suite runs two tests at a time, each connecting to the
    display, and a test which starts as the last other one exits fails at once. This failed 2 of 30 builds in GitLab
    CI, both in test-file-saver. Running the test target as the build does, on 2 CPUs, 1 of 200 runs failed, and in
    Xvfb's log (-audit 4) the failing test never connected, right after every other client had disconnected. Of 160
    runs in 4 loops side by side on one CPU each, 8 failed this way with Xvfb's default and none of 160 with
    -noreset.

    The patch passes -noreset, with xvfb-run's default screen, as many Debian packages do for Debian bug 981201
    (https://bugs.debian.org/981201), which asks for -noreset to be xvfb-run's default. Debian's packaging, which
    Ubuntu syncs, still runs the tests without it in 5.22.0-2. Drop the patch once Ubuntu's gtksourceview5 or
    xvfb-run passes -noreset.
